end group


==Migration==
autonumber 2.3
group Migration - __init__ constructor 
    Migration -> Migration: Create a variable self.db and store instance of Database class
    Migration -> Session: 
        Session -> Session: Create a protected variable instance and aassign None
        group Database - __new__ constructor 
            alt if cls._instance == None
                Session -> Session: Call the super() class of __new__ to create new object and store in variable _instance of class cls 
                Session -> Session: Create a protected variable for class cls as initialized and assign false
            else 
                Session -> Session: Return the instance of class cls
            end 
        end group
        group Database - __init__ constructor 
            alt if initialized == true
                Session -> Session: If an object for the class Database is already initialized return
            else 
                Session -> Session: Create a variable engine for the object and call the function _create_engine
                group Database _create_engine()
                    Session -> Session: Create a variable db_url and store the url for database by using the db credentials from settings.py file and return the db_url  
                end group
                Session -> Session: Create a variable SessioonLocal and store instance for class Sessionmaker by providing db url for enginne and defining autoflush and autocommit
                Session -> Session: Assign the variable initialized as True as no other instance  is created for the class Database  
            end
        end group 
    Migration <-- Session: 
    group create_tables()
            group Try
                Migration -> Migration: Using the class Base create the tables in database using the database engine
            end group
            group Except
                Migration -> Migration: If any error raises while creating databse, raise the error
            end group
    end group
end group

