group place_order_tool() 
        Tools -> Tools: Create instance for ChatBotRepository and store in a variable repository
    group Try
        Tools -> Tools: This tool place order for customers by providing the required parameters like list of items, ad their count in list and the customer_id
        Tools -> Tools: Iterate over the list, which stores the item_id and check the presence of item in the menu by using the function validate_item() and calculate the total price of order
        Tools -> Repository
        group validate_item(item_id) function
            Repository-> Repository: Create a variable db_session and store the connection session with database
            Repository -> Repository: Create a variable  product and assign orm query to validate whether the item asked by the customer is present or not
            note left
            **ORM Query**
                query(Item).filter(Item.item_id == item_id).first()
            end note
            Repository -> Repository: Return the product to tools
        end group
        Repository --> Tools
        alt if product not found
            Tools -> Tools: If item asked by customer is not found in the menu, return the custom message to the LLM
        else
            Tools -> Tools: If items present, call the place_order_repository() function in repository to place order with required parameters item_id, count, total_amount and customer_id
            Tools -> Repository:
        end
        group place_order_repository(item_id, count, total_amount, customer_id) 
            group Try
                Repository-> Repository: CAll from tools place_order_tool() trigger ths function place_order_repository() to place the order
                ' activate Repository
                Repository-> Repository: Create a variable db_session and store the connection session with database
                Repository <- Session:
                activate Session
                    Repository -> Repository: Create a variable customer and call the function get_customer() with parameter customer_id
                    group get_customer(customer_id)
                        group Try
                            Repository-> Repository: Create a variable db_session and store the connection session with database
                            Repository-> Repository: Create a variable customer and assign the query to get the details of customer with customer_id as in parameter
                            note left
                            **ORM Query**
                                query(Customer).filter(Customer.customer_id == customer_id).first()
                            end note
                        end group
                        group Except as e
                            Repository-> Repository: Refer the except group of function place_order_repository()
                        end group
                        group Finally
                            Repository-> Repository: Close the database connection session, which is stored in variable db_session
                        end group
                    end group
                    Repository-> Repository: Create a variable new_order and add the total_amount, customer_id and the customer name  of the order and then perform flush to create instance  of new record in orders table 
                    note left
                    **ORM Query**
                        new_order = Order(
                            customer_id = customer_id,
                            total_amount = total_amount,
                            created_by = customer.name
                        )
                    end note 
                    Repository-> Repository: Iterate over the list item_id and count to add the each item of the order with its order_id to create instance for  class Order_Item table definition
                    note left
                    **ORM Query**
                        new_order_items = Order_Item(
                            order_id = order.order_id,
                            item_id =  item,
                            item_count = cnt,
                        )
                    end note 
                    Repository-> Repository: After each iteration, add all the orm object to list order_item and do commit after final iteration to add records in database tables
                    Repository -> Session:
                deactivate Session 
                Repository-> Repository: Return the order_id & total amount with custom message to tool place_order_tool()
                Repository--> Tools:
                ' deactivate Repository
            end group
            group Except as e
                    Repository -> Repository: Call the utility function error_logger() by sending the parameters file_name, function_name and error_message 'e' to create an error log in database
                    Repository -> ErrorLogger: Any error raise, triggers the function error_logger() to create db record for error
                    group error_logger(file_name, function_name, error_message)
                        activate ErrorLogger
                        ErrorLogger -> ErrorLogger: create an instance for class ErrorLog and store in a variable repository
                        ErrorLogger -> ErrorLogger: Passes the incoming parameters to add_errorlog_repository function in error_repository to create a db record for error
                        ErrorLogger -> ErrorLogRepository:
                        activate ErrorLogRepository
                    end group
                    group add_errorlog_repository(file_name, function_name, error_message)
                        ErrorLogRepository -> ErrorLogRepository: create a variable db_instance and store the instance for class Database
                        ErrorLogRepository -> ErrorLogRepository: Create a variable db_session and store the database seesion
                        ErrorLogRepository -> ErrorLogRepository: create a variable error and assign the values to be insrted into database as instance for class Error_Logger and perform add & commit to save the changes in database
                        ErrorLogRepository -> ErrorLogRepository: Return the success message as True to error_logger function
                        ErrorLogRepository --> ErrorLogger
                        deactivate ErrorLogRepository
                    end group
                    ErrorLogger --> Repository:  Return the success message from function add_errorlog_repository to router 
                    deactivate ErrorLogger
                        Repository -> Repository: Create Custom Exception instance with assigning error message to message,error code to variable code and stsatus code to variable status_code 
                        Repository -> CustomException: Constructs CustomException with an error message and status code 
                        activate CustomException
                            CustomException -> CustomException: assigns the error message in variable message
                            CustomException -> ErrorCodes : Maps the errror code "INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR"
                            ErrorCodes --> CustomException: Returns the error code "InternalServerErrorCode"
                            CustomException -> HttpStatus : Map status code alligns with the error cod "INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR" 
                            HttpStatus --> CustomException: Returns the status code 500
                            CustomException -> CustomException: variable request_id generates and store a uuid id and store in strong format 
                            CustomException --> Repository: Raise Custom Exception object
                        deactivate CustomException
