group get_order_tool() 
    group Try 
        Tools -> Tools: This tool get_order_tool() gets the status of the order to the customer
        Tools -> Tools: Call the function get_order_detail_repository() in repositories file to get the status or the order by sending thr customer_id as parameter and store in variable result
        Tools -> Repository:
        ' activate Repository
            group get_order_detail_repository(self, customer_id) 
                group Try
                    Repository-> Repository: CAll from tool get_order_tool() trigger the function get_order_detail_repository() to get status of the order
                    Repository-> Repository: Create a variable customer and call the function get_customer() by sending customer_id as parameter
                    group get_customer(customer_id) 
                        group Try
                            Repository-> Repository: Create a variable customer and assign the query to get the details of customer with customer_id as in parameter
                            note left
                            **ORM Query**
                                query(Customer).filter(Customer.customer_id == customer_id)
                                .first()
                            end note
                            Repository-> Repository: Return the customer sql object
                        end group
                        group Except as e
                            Repository-> Repository: Refer the except group of function place_order_repository()
                        end group
                        group Finally
                            Repository-> Repository: Close the database connection session, which is stored in variable db_session
                        end group
                    end group
                    Repository-> Repository: Create a variable order and call the function get_order by sending the parameter customer_id
                    group get_order(customer_id)
                        group Try
                            Repository-> Repository: Create a variable order and assign the query to get the details of order with customer_id as in parameter
                            note left
                            **ORM Query**
                                query(Order).filter(Order.customer_id == customer_id)
                                .order_by(desc(Order.created_at)).first()
                            end note
                            Repository-> Repository: Return the order sql object
                        end group
                        group Except as e
                            Repository-> Repository: Refer the except group of function place_order_repository()
                        end group
                        group Finally
                            Repository-> Repository: Close the database connection session, which is stored in variable db_session
                        end group
                    end group
                    Repository-> Repository: Create a variable order_details and call the function get_order_details() to get the sql_object of the order record with order_id
                    alt if no order available
                        Repository-> Repository: if there is no sql_object found with  order_id, return a custom message about no order found on the give order_id to the tool get_order_tool().
                    end
                    group get_order_details(order_id)
                        group Try
                            Repository-> Repository: Create a variable order_details and assign the query to get the details of order with order_id as in parameter
                            note left
                            **ORM Query**
                                db_session.query(Order_Item)
                                .filter(Order_Item.order_id == order_id)
                                .all()
                            end note
                            Repository-> Repository: Return the order_details sql object
                        end group
                        group Except as e
                            Repository-> Repository: Refer the except group of function place_order_repository()
                        end group
                        group Finally
                            Repository-> Repository: Close the database connection session, which is stored in variable db_session
                        end group
                    end group
                    Repository-> Repository: Iterate over the sql object in variable in order_details and store the data like item_id, namae and count indictionary and append it to list 
                    Repository-> Repository: If sql_object for order_id found , return the status of the order, total amount and list of order item detail of order with custom message to tool  get_order_tool() 
                    Repository--> Tools:
                end group
                group Except as e
                    Repository-> Repository: Refer sequence number 24 to 45 for error handling and logging the error in repository function get_order_detail_repository
                end group
                group Finally
                    Repository-> Repository: Close the database connection session, which is stored in variable db_session
                end group
            end group
        Tools -> Tools: The return message with order status is sent to LLM, it process the input and responses the users requests 
    end group
    group Except as e
        Tools -> Tools: Refer sequence number 24 to 45 for error logging and exception handling in tool
    end group
end group


